% FULL TEXT READ 11 Sep 2026 (IOPscience PDF, 15 pp). This is the concrete
% published procedure Chapter 1 needed. What it actually does, verbatim:
%   Sec. 3.2  infers Te from the D 9->2 / 5->2 intensity ratio, populations from
%             ADAS PECs. Fig. 4(a) is drawn at an ASSUMED neutral fraction
%             n_0/n_e = 0.50; Fig. 4(b) plots the ratio against Te AND the
%             neutral fraction. The neutral-to-ion ratio is therefore NOT
%             eliminated: it is carried as an unknown.
%   Sec. 3.2  "it is possible for the measured line ratio value to correspond to
%             different temperatures, if the extent of the excitation
%             contribution is not known" -> the same non-uniqueness this thesis
%             finds independently.
%   Sec. 3.2  bracketing n_0/n_e over 0.1-0.8 gives Te = 1.8-2.5 eV, quoted as
%             an UPPER limit on Te, not a value.
%   Sec. 3.2  the closure finally adopted is that the ratio is "mainly driven by
%             recombination processes in detached plasmas", following Lumma1997
%             and McCracken1998, and it is available because "the contribution
%             due to excitation is negligible for n_upper > 5 for Te < 2 eV for
%             any reasonable values of the neutral fraction".
